        "paired_field_energy_has_an_exact_positive_conserved_form"
      ],
      "scope_boundary": "Explicit positive invariant for the full pair update, and separate balanced invariants on its source sector. Native matching squares prove positivity; no classical field energy or physical energy identification is supplied."
    },
    {
      "id": "R29.5",
      "title": "The source field has an exact local current and a visible defect source",
      "written_section_sha256": "76b6c03be4f87865dbfe424d261573132728b4cca059ff73813f94364059177a",
      "evidence": "WRITTEN_NATIVE_PROOF_WITH_SCOPED_EXACT_CHECKS",
      "exact_check_groups": [
        "local_field_current_is_a_complete_quadratic_identity"
      ],
      "scope_boundary": "Complete finite quadratic current identity and its exact compatibility-source correction. Source-field energy conservation is local as well as global; physical current and electric charge remain unidentified."
    },
    {
      "id": "R29.6",
      "title": "Zero-field backgrounds are exactly the stationary uniform sector",
      "written_section_sha256": "769a5395c2467c3d0ff32ae789cf8a893b39ccf911ad846d419c09f1aeeff5e7",
      "evidence": "WRITTEN_NATIVE_PROOF_WITH_SCOPED_EXACT_CHECKS",
      "exact_check_groups": [
        "cyclic_zero_field_backgrounds_have_exactly_two_native_kernel_roles",
        "source_transport_factors_into_a_native_constitutive_operator"
      ],
      "scope_boundary": "Uniform potentials are exactly the stationary two-event, zero-difference-field backgrounds. The observer forgets only a global native two-role offset. No infinite background norm, arbitrary local gauge symmetry or physical vacuum is assumed."
    },
    {
      "id": "R29.7",
      "title": "An interface between zero-field backgrounds has a conserved boundary residue",
      "written_section_sha256": "8d8ba36cdec58966c3962b8ea7019a2c62fc92ccc83194b28caa1df2ffcebf76",
      "evidence": "WRITTEN_NATIVE_PROOF_WITH_SCOPED_EXACT_CHECKS",
      "exact_check_groups": [
        "boundary_interface_residue_and_native_width_bound_are_exact",
        "finite_difference_fields_reconstruct_their_source_without_extra_modes"
      ],
      "scope_boundary": "Finite field differences reconstruct constant-tail native sequences. End mismatch is conserved, zero mismatch can radiate in this mathematical target, and an exact width bound rules out selecting mass from boundary residue alone. No physical charge quantization follows."
    }
